course: dictionary
lesson: 8570
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The context, the words and sentences around it, shows you which meaning the writer wants. «The scene was painted by a famous artist.» Here scene is a picture of a place, a view you can look at.
explain: In a story, play or film, a scene is one part shown at one place and time. A new scene often means the place or time has changed. When you meet scene, ask: is this a picture, a part of a story, or a place where something happened?
explain: The word can also mean the place where something happened, like «the scene of an accident». In that sense it is a safety word: stay back and let the helpers do their work. Choose the meaning that fits the clues, then check it by putting your meaning into the sentence.
fact: A scene is one part of a story, play or film, shown at one place and time.
fact: A scene can also be a view you can see, such as «a winter scene».
fact: «Scene» can mean the place where something happened, such as the scene of an accident.
fact: In a play, each scene starts from zero, like a round of things put on and taken off the table.
fact: «To make a scene» means to make a fuss in public.
exercise: «The scene was painted by a famous artist.» What does scene mean here? | A picture of a view | A part of a play | A fuss in public | *A painted view you can look at
exercise: «A clapperboard shows the scene and take number.» What is a take? | The name of the film | A type of camera | The last scene of the film | *One try at filming a shot
exercise: «Scene: at Christmas dinner in Leeds, Grandad and Auntie Jo argue about the government until the gravy goes cold.» Why is this called a scene? | *It is one part of a story shown at one place and time | It is a fuss about the gravy | It is a view of snow | It is a painting of a kitchen
test: Ella says «the scene of the accident» means a film scene. What does it mean? | A painting of a road | *A place where something happened, and where helpers must work, so stay back | A place where something happened | A camera for filming
test: «A winter scene» is in the art class. What does scene mean here? | A part of a play | To make a fuss | *A view you can see | One try at filming a shot
exam: Ahmed says «to make a scene» means to paint a picture. Is he right? | Yes, it means to film | *No, it means to make a fuss in public | No, it means to run away | Yes, it means to paint
